name gun-turning-1
timeout 400

# THE HARD GUN CASE: the same armed pursuer as gun-bfm.fbm against bfm-basic.fbm's TURNING defender.
#
# gun-bfm is a tracking pass — the defender flies a straight line, so the required lead is nearly
# constant and a pilot that gets the nose there once keeps it there. This mission removes exactly that
# one property and nothing else: the defender flies bfm-basic's sustained max-rate level left turn
# (one waypoint at the CENTRE of its own turn circle, a point FBAutopilot::Direct can never reach, so
# the orbit is steady and reproducible — measured at 58.9 deg of bank, 4.7 deg/s, ~1,880 m radius).
#
# WHAT THAT DOES TO THE SHOOTER, and why this file exists: against a turning target the EEGS lead
# solution SWEEPS through the funnel. Measured on this geometry, the aiming error moves at roughly two
# degrees per second while the rounds need 0.3-0.9 s to arrive, so a pursuit law that only regulates
# the ERROR carries a steady-state lag of (error rate x its own time constant) and squeezes on a
# solution that has already moved on. The fix is a tracking loop in which the error RATE is a control
# term of its own (systems/FBPilot's gun-tracking law), and this mission is where that is measured:
#
#   gun_sol_err / gun_in_funnel   the aiming error and the funnel bit as a time series — the two
#                                 numbers the tracking loop is judged on (mean error while tracking,
#                                 seconds inside the funnel)
#   pilot GUN_TRACK / GUN_BREAK   every entry into and exit out of the funnel-flying law
#   gun TRIGGER / BURST / HIT     every squeeze, every bundle, and what reached the airframe
#   damage SYSTEM / KILL          what those rounds took out
#
# THE RUN ENDS IN A KILL, exit 1 at t=52.1: the defender's flight controls and structure fail together
# under the second squeeze and its own mission monitor concludes FAIL ("combat ineffective"). exit 1 is
# the PASSING outcome — with a pursuit law that regulates only the ERROR this same geometry never put a
# single round on the airframe in 400 s, so a run that reaches its timeout means the tracking loop has
# regressed. The detail is read from the events and the telemetry, not from the exit code.
#
# GEOMETRY AT T=0 is gun-bfm's, to the digit: viper 2 nm dead astern, co-altitude, nose on, at the
# model's measured corner speed (380 KCAS, `make test-corner`).

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.67485 6.85148 4000 90.0 380       # 2 nm in trail, co-altitude, corner speed
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off                           # no net: the fight is flown on the radar alone
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                       # the 30x20 auto-locking ACM box
  set task bfm
  set brief_master_arm arm                   # entered over the bus once airborne, like every brief item
  set pilot_bfm_ctrl_min_nm 0.15             # the guns control position (see gun-bfm.fbm's header)
  set pilot_bfm_ctrl_max_nm 0.40
  wp 46.70000 6.90000 4000 380               # the nav solution the fire control needs, never steered to

unit bandit
  module f16
  team hostile
  spawn 46.67485 6.90000 4000 90.0 300       # 2 nm ahead of viper, entering its break turn
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off                           # the defender is a target, it does not look
  wp 46.70000 6.90000 4000 300               # the CENTRE of its turn — see bfm-basic.fbm's header
